      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4b6c50e21cea065ff2dcee64c981a7997a4b7f8464d2ee1526a269b91ee6ba06",
      "skos:note": "Granting powers to the Commissioner"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-office-of-the-privacy-commissioner-act-2000#sch-1-sec-26a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26A(2) Staff and consultants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 6,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Commissioner has all the powers of, or exercisable by, a\nSecretary under that Act, so far as those powers relate to the branch\nof the Australian Public Service comprising the staff mentioned in\nsubsection (1), as if that branch were a separate Department of the\nAustralian Public Service.\n\nOffice of the Privacy Commissioner  Schedule 1\nPrivacy Act 1988  Part 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Office of the Privacy Commissioner) Act 2000                   3"
    },
